    Bug 2039908 - DeCOMtaminate internal nsMsgDBView methods NoteChange and GetFolderForViewIndex. r=mkmelin


    This patch removes unnecessary XPCOM overhead from methods that are strictly
    internal to the C++ view hierarchy.

    - `GetFolderForViewIndex` now returns a raw `nsIMsgFolder*` (borrowing contract)
      directly, instead of returning an `nsresult` and passing the folder via an
      `nsIMsgFolder**` out-parameter. This completely eliminates the forced `AddRef`/
      `Release` cycles, particularly the legacy workaround used with `EntryInfo2`.

    - `NoteChange` now returns `void` instead of `nsresult`, as tree invalidation
      has no meaningful failure state for callers to handle.

    - C++ callers have been updated to use fast pointer null-checks (`NS_ENSURE_TRUE`)
      instead of `NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS`.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300785

